/*
 * Filigree style "Clean Briar": a thorned briar stem along each edge with a
 * few leaves and closed buds, the closest of the briar families to the
 * original Thorned Bramble. Six corner pieces, exported from the generator
 * page at design/thorn-corners/ (family `briar`; see its README to
 * regenerate) and copied here verbatim as path data: all solid
 * `currentColor` fills, no strokes. A path string that starts with "E:" is
 * drawn with fill-rule="evenodd"; Clean Briar has none, but FiligreeCorners
 * supports them.
 *
 * Unlike the single-piece styles, this one exports CORNER_PIECES instead of
 * CornerArt: FiligreeCorners picks one piece per corner and may mirror it
 * across the diagonal (see ../Filigree.jsx). It has no divider of its own:
 * ./index.js gives it Thorned Bramble's. Plain data with no JSX, so Node
 * scripts (scripts/design-check.mjs) can import CORNER_SIZE from it.
 */

/* Corners are drawn 112px, the same scale as the bramble ones (scale.js). */
export const CORNER_SIZE = 112;
/*
 * The 100-unit box less its empty top and left edge (no piece draws within
 * 8 units of either), so the corner box reaches about 17px outside the frame
 * instead of 22px and a framed box near a 390px page's edge does not scroll
 * it sideways. The artwork and its scale are unchanged.
 */
export const CORNER_VIEWBOX = "5 5 95 95";

/*
 * Frame metrics, as in bramble.jsx: a 2px frame line whose corner is at
 * (20,20) in the 100 box. The arms reach up to about 99 units along each
 * edge, so a framed box should be at least FRAME_MIN_SPAN corner sizes (about
 * 180px) tall and wide, or the arms along one edge run into each other.
 */
export const FRAME_BORDER = "border-2";
export const FRAME_BORDER_WIDTH = 2;
export const FRAME_INSET = 0.2;
export const FRAME_MIN_SPAN = 1.6;

